(4. Service levels) Tj T*
(4.1. The Supplier shall use reasonable efforts to keep the platform available.) Tj T*
(4.2. Planned maintenance may be carried out at any time with 24 hours' notice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Liability) Tj T*
(5.1. The Supplier's total liability under this Agreement shall not exceed the fees paid by the) Tj T*
(Client in the one month preceding the event giving rise to the claim.) Tj T*
(5.2. The Client shall be liable without limitation for any damage caused to the Supplier,) Tj T*
(including lost profits.) Tj T*
(5.3. The Client shall indemnify the Supplier against all claims of third parties related to the) Tj T*
(content hosted on the platform.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Intellectual property) Tj T*
(6.1. All software, configurations and scripts developed by the Supplier under this Agreement,) Tj T*
(including those paid for by the Client, remain the exclusive property of the Supplier.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. Exclusivity) Tj T*
(7.1. During the term of this Agreement the Client shall not engage any other provider for) Tj T*
(hosting or maintenance services.) Tj T*
(7.2. In case of breach of clause 7.1 the Client shall pay a penalty of EUR 50,000.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. Confidentiality) Tj T*
(8.1. Each party shall keep confidential all information received from the other party.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(9. Governing law) Tj T*
(9.1. This Agreement is governed by the laws of the Republic of Bulgaria. Disputes shall be) Tj T*
(resolved by the competent court in Sofia.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(10. Kick-off) Tj T*
(10.1. The Client shall provide administrator access to the current platform by 20 November) Tj T*
(2026.) Tj T*
(10.2. The first monthly report shall be delivered by 5 January 2027.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Supplier: Northwind Cloud Ltd.                Client: Brightline Retail AD) Tj T*
